#  Nothing in this list may ever be committed.  Git history is permanent: a file
#  removed in a later commit is still downloadable from the earlier one, so the
#  only safe moment to catch these is before the first `git add`.

#  --- credentials -----------------------------------------------------------
mp_key.txt
*.key
.env

#  --- third-party copyrighted material --------------------------------------
#  The Landolt-Boernstein volumes, the Akgun-Ugur papers and the other journal
#  PDFs are publisher copyright.  Individual measured constants are facts and
#  are cited normally in refdata.py; the volumes themselves are not ours to
#  redistribute, and neither is text extracted wholesale from them.
*.pdf
LB13a_text.json
LB13a_index.json
gulp-*.gz
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

#  --- bulk run output -------------------------------------------------------
#  Search output is large, uninteresting and regenerable.  fit.json is the
#  distilled result and IS tracked.
runs/
rc3test/
hcptest/
dense_*.json
log_*.txt
*-[0-9]*.out
*-[0-9]*.err

#  --- large derived data ----------------------------------------------------
#  library.json is ~4 MB and is rebuilt by refresh.py from fit.json in a few
#  minutes; docs/index.html already carries everything a reader needs.
library.json
mfp_all.json
*_phonon.json

#  --- the long-form notes ---------------------------------------------------
#  Not published.  Excluding only the .docx would miss the point: the builder
#  scripts carry the entire text inline, so they are excluded too.
doc/
*.docx
HANDBOOK.md

#  --- housekeeping ----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
_probe*.docx
*.bak
*.pre-*
